// PyPilot task templates (F6).
//
// Zed extensions cannot register custom command-palette entries, so the palette
// surface is provided through tasks: `task: spawn` lists these by label.
//
// Install by copying into either:
//   * global: ~/.config/zed/tasks.json   (Windows: %APPDATA%\Zed\tasks.json)
//   * project: <workspace>/.zed/tasks.json
//
// Labels mirror the F5 toast buttons so the two surfaces map 1:1:
//   "Fix everything" runs pypilot setup   (identical code path)
//   "Show details"   runs pypilot doctor  (same assessment, read-only)
//
// We deliberately pass NO `--path`: Zed sets `cwd` to the worktree root and
// pypilot defaults to the current directory, so paths containing spaces can
// never be split by shell word-splitting.
//
// Windows notes (speed + correctness):
//   * If task spawn fails with "os error 193 (%1 is not a valid Win32
//     application)": Zed's spawner cannot launch Microsoft Store *App
//     Execution Aliases* (0-byte reparse points), even though plain
//     CreateProcess can. This rules out bare "pwsh.exe" AND every
//     WindowsApps pwsh path when PowerShell 7 came from the Store. Pin a
//     real PE at a stable path instead. System32 PowerShell always exists,
//     never moves, and with -NoProfile is the fastest shell spawn:
//       "shell": {
//         "with_arguments": {
//           "program": "C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe",
//           "args": ["-NoProfile"]
//         }
//       }
//     (If PowerShell 7 came from MSI or winget rather than the Store, then
//     "C:\\Program Files\\PowerShell\\7\\pwsh.exe" is a real PE at a stable
//     path and works too.)
//   * -NoProfile matters either way: task spawns are non-interactive, so
//     skipping the profile (prompt/banner tooling) roughly halves startup.
[
  {
    "label": "pypilot: fix everything (set up environment)",
    "command": "pypilot",
    "args": ["setup"],
    "cwd": "$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT",
    "use_new_terminal": false,
    "allow_concurrent_runs": false,
    "save": "all",
    "reveal": "always"
  },
  {
    "label": "pypilot: show details (doctor report)",
    "command": "pypilot",
    "args": ["doctor"],
    "cwd": "$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT",
    "use_new_terminal": false,
    "allow_concurrent_runs": false,
    "reveal": "always"
  }
]
